glibc has no getdents(); use getdents64() (glibc >= 2.30), whose buffer
layout matches glibc's struct dirent. The SYS_getdents shims used in
dinit-chimera#34 and Casuarina return the legacy linux_dirent layout
(d_type after the name), which misparses every entry name.

--- a/src/shared/copy.c
+++ b/src/shared/copy.c
@@ -908,7 +908,7 @@
                 struct dirent *de;
                 ssize_t n;

-                n = getdents(fd, buf, m);
+                n = getdents64(fd, buf, m);
                 if (n < 0)
                         return -errno;
                 if (n == 0)
